{"availability":"available","full":"llmmanorg/llmman","name":"llmman","description":"Run any agent on any model, models stored as OCI images","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":544,"forks":68,"created":"2026-03-22T01:27:35Z","updated":"2026-10-08T23:33:52Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://llmmanorg.github.io/","topics":["claude-code","codex","llama-cpp","llm","mlx","oci","opencode","vllm"],"demo":"https://llmmanorg.github.io/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:04.660Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:04.660Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:04.660Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:51.171Z","stars":540,"forks":69},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:04.660Z","stars":544,"forks":68}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode and friends, pointed at a model running on your own machine, or at any hosted provider, in one command.","That starts a local inference server, fetches the tested llama.cpp release for your GPU (as a container on Linux with Docker or Podman, otherwise a prebuilt binary), loads the model, and execs an agent against it.","Models are OCI images, so moving one takes no tooling you don't already have:"],"features":["Provider agnostic. The same launch, run and list commands work","Registry agnostic. llmman run qwen3.8 pulls straight from Docker","Vanilla everything. Upstream llama.cpp releases (or the","One-step transfer. Any source pull understands paired with any OCI","Pool your machines. Several llmman serve daemons form an"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/llmmanorg/llmman/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"985ae4ac36d9379eb644bb37d47d46a1a1a718dfee697884dcf7aa3b8caf11eb","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:05.054Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:05.054Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode and friends, pointed at a model running on your own machine, or at any hosted provider, in one command.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/llmmanorg/llmman/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Or package a model as a plain OCI artifact and push it to GHCR, quay, Harbor or a self-hosted mirror, then llmman run it from there.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/llmmanorg/llmman/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No curated library, no account with llmman, no gatekeeper.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/llmmanorg/llmman/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"A daemon the network can reach requires an API key on every request (LLMMANAPIKEYS, or auth.apikeys as above; the CLI sends LLMMANAPIKEY) unless LLMMANAUTH=off, and can terminate TLS itself with LLMMANTLSCERT/LLMMANTLSKEY.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/llmmanorg/llmman/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"GitHub Copilot uses the standalone copilot CLI (npm install -g @github/copilot) in BYOK mode, so a local-model launch does not require a GitHub login.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/llmmanorg/llmman/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"AGY requires version 1.1.13 or newer for Gemini API-key and custom-endpoint support. llmman writes Gemini mode to its own stable settings directory at /.gemini/llmman/; your AGY settings stay untouched.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/llmmanorg/llmman/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"985ae4ac36d9379eb644bb37d47d46a1a1a718dfee697884dcf7aa3b8caf11eb","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/llmmanorg/llmman/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:05.054Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T23:33:52Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/llmmanorg/llmman/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:05.056Z","hash":"985ae4ac36d9379eb644bb37d47d46a1a1a718dfee697884dcf7aa3b8caf11eb","originalBytes":18132,"storedByt